    <h2 id="time-to-think_7049024273555">Time to Think</h2>
    <p>As you work through the course, you will be presented with a number of Time to Think boxes. Please watch this video which will show you how to use these and why they are important.</p>

    <!-- all.njk VIDEO 2 -->
    
    
      <div class="l-video-container">
        <video poster="~/images/svg/poster.svg" controls preload="metadata" aria-labelledby="time-to-think_7049024273555" width="1000"
          data-base="cs-time-to-think" 
          data-ext=".mp4" 
          data-multi="false"
          data-trans="cs-time-to-think undefined">
          <source src="https://kpcontent.blob.core.windows.net/$web/resources/v2l/720/cs-time-to-think.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          <track default label="English" kind="captions" srclang="en" src="~/videos/captions/vtt/cs-time-to-think.vtt">
          <p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos</p>
        </video>
      </div>
      
          <toggle-section open="false">
            <h3>Video transcript </h3>
            <p><strong>Lloyd:</strong> Hi, and welcome to the short video which will explain the purpose of the Time to Think boxes.</p>
<p>So now that you've started your course, you will be on page one of session one, and I would strongly suggest that you familiarise yourself with the icons on the page, which will appear at different points throughout the course. And they relate to certain things such as Key Points, Stretches and the Time to Thinks, Case Studies, Watch and Reads. And then you have the video which will explain submitting assessments. If you have any difficulty with this, if you just Vmail your tutor and they will explain how to go about submitting your assessments correctly. And then you have the Time to Think video, which is what you're watching now.</p>
<p>And once you've done that, if you go to page 2, this then brings you to your Learning Goals page and it will give you all of the learning goals and you can download the actual full criteria for this unit. And then a little bit of an introduction, all about goal setting and creating a motivation map, and then the hints and tips, which I would strongly suggest downloading because they will assist you when you come to do your assessment.</p>
<p>And then page 3, you are starting the first page of the course materials. So as you work through each of the pages and each of the sessions for each unit we will watch the videos, the video transcripts are there, there are quizzes. There's another video there. And then you'll come to the Time to Thinks.</p>
<p>So what you can do with these is in the Time to Thinks you can access these from your journal. So whatever you type in here will be saved. And then in your journal, you will be able to access that. And I strongly suggest that you do complete these Time to Thinks. So quite a lot of them are linked to the assessment questions, so the more information that you put into your Time to Thinks, the easier it will be when you come to do your actual assessment questions.</p>
<p>And as I said, there's two Time to Thinks on that page. All you would do... type something in there, click save, and then that will go to your journal. And then on the My Course page, so if I just go back to the top, go to the My Course page and as you can see, I have my journal here. So if I click on the journal, you'll be able to see that, my note there -- &quot;hello&quot; -- it was in there. So for every day, every time you enter a journal entry, It will be showing up in the little calendar there. So you can then navigate through them. As I say it, I would strongly urge you to complete them because they will assist you when you complete the assessment.</p>

          </toggle-section>
        
      
  
</section>

  





